{"results": [{"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-058", "score": 0.118, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-058 | Study family SF-APPS-058: Observed on-ball defensive scheme labels (ORL-DET G1)\n- observed_research_question: Observed on-ball defensive scheme labels (ORL-DET G1)\n- auto_outcome_status: untestable\n- observed_hypothesis: NBA matchup/PBP fields can label on-ball coverage (DROP/ICE/SWITCH) at usable rates.\n- observed_result: DET: 67 on-ball HC poss, 10 labeled (14.9%) ? DROP n=5 PPP=1.20, ICE_CANDIDATE n=5 PPP=0.80, OTHER n=57 PPP=1.42. ORL: 60 poss, 2 labeled (3.3%). switches_on unpopulated.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:label_or_classification_error\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:LABEL_ERROR\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER\n- observed_failure_evidence: Confident label rates 14.9% and 3.3%; NBA matchups feed did not populate switches_on.\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=67/60 possessions, 10/2 labeled\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- observed_verdict: failed_gate"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-CHT-039", "score": 0.105, "document": "# FAM:SF-CHT-039 | Study family SF-CHT-039: Series-level AVOID share vs winning (talent confound)\n- observed_research_question: Series-level AVOID share vs winning (talent confound)\n- auto_outcome_status: untestable\n- observed_hypothesis: Higher AVOID share predicts losing, independent of team quality.\n- observed_result: Game-level rho=-0.19 p=0.008 (inflated n, team-quality confound). Series-level rho=-0.26 p=0.07 (n=50, underpowered; ~80 series needed for p<0.05). Low AVOID-share bin 52.6% vs 25-50% bin 37.0%.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:confounding\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:CONFOUNDING\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER\n- observed_failure_evidence: Series n=50 p=0.07; still confounded by team quality (OKC disciplined and good).\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=50 series; stated need ~80 for p<0.05\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- observed_verdict: inconclusive"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-CHT-016", "score": 0.099, "document": "# FAM:SF-CHT-016 | Study family SF-CHT-016: Holdout leakage audit of fitted pipeline parameters\n- observed_research_question: Holdout leakage audit of fitted pipeline parameters\n- auto_outcome_status: not a hypothesis test\n- observed_hypothesis: Pooled splits feed holdout information into fitted calibrator/kernel parameters.\n- observed_result: Zero true leakage paths for the predictive calibrator (fit on VAL with TRAIN-only features; HOLDOUT never in coefficient estimation). Two external constants (playoff scalars, PNR-drop tier bands) could carry implicit exp [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: D_positive (no failure: positive result)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:leakage\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:LEAKAGE_LOOKAHEAD\n- observed_failure_evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- observed_sample_and_power: 17 parameters enumerated\n- observed_method: Enumerated 17 fitted/calibrated/aggregate params and their fit splits.\n- observed_verdict: tool_eval_pass\n- observed_failure_type: D_positive"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-001", "score": 0.085, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-001 | Study family SF-APPS-001: Overnight 10-series LLM adaptation review (adapters win series)\n- observed_research_question: Overnight 10-series LLM adaptation review (adapters win series)\n- auto_outcome_status: not a hypothesis test\n- observed_hypothesis: The team that adapted better within games (per LLM adaptation review) wins the playoff series.\n- observed_result: Team judged to have adapted better won 9 of 10 series; exception RECENT3_DEN_vs_MIN_26. SPOT_UP and DRIVE stifled in 10/10 series; offenses failed to counter in 9/10.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY\n- observed_failure_evidence: Post-hoc LLM narrative judgment of 'adapted better' with knowledge of winners; several winners described as adapting better 'enough (or opponent failed more)'.\n- observed_sample_and_power: 10 series, 104 team-game reports; per-half play-type samples often n<10 possessions\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED"}], "n_results": 4}

Stage 2. Using the retrieval result above (follow-up tools are allowed within the tool budget), complete steps 4 to 9
and reply with the final action. Output schema (all fields required):
{
 "research_concepts": [
